# No catch-all file searches

Never use a `*` / `**/*` glob, or an unscoped regex, that walks the entire repository. That pull includes `.venv/`, `venv/`, `var/` (logs, SQLite, checkpoints, CAD downloads), `web/node_modules/`, `__pycache__/`, and other generated junk.

## Do not

- Glob tool: `glob_pattern: "*"` or `"**/*"` from the repo root
- Grep/ripgrep from the repo root with no `path` and no tight `glob`
- `Get-ChildItem -Recurse` (or `rg` / `dir /s`) from the repo root without excludes

## Do

- List only the directory you need (`Get-ChildItem -Name`, no recurse)
- Scope searches: `python/talongym/**/*.py`, `web/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`, `docs/*.md`, `tests/**/*.py`
- Open known paths (`README.md`, `pyproject.toml`) instead of discovering them with `*`

Stay out of `.venv/`, `venv/`, `var/`, `logs/`, `outputs/`, `web/node_modules/`, `web/dist/`, `engine/target/`, `.pytest_cache/`, and `__pycache__/`.
